//STAFF OF COMMAND +3 - 10000mo//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/STAF09.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Staff"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "The simplest and humblest of staff weapons, the quarterstaff is a length of wood ranging six to nine feet in length. High-quality quarterstaves are made of stout oak and are shod with metal at both ends. The quarterstaff must be wielded with both hands.

STATISTICS:

Damage: 1d6 (crushing)
Speed Factor: 4
Proficiency Type: Quarterstaff
Type: Two-handed
Requires:
 5 Strength

Weight: 4"

	SAY NAME2 "Staff of Command +3"
	SAY DESC "Whispers in the dark corners of Faerûn speak of a slender, obsidian rod that hungers for the autonomy of others. Its origins are entirely lost to the mists of time; no sage can name the wizard who forged it, nor the kingdom where it first brought monarchs to their knees. What is certain is its lineage of blood and subjugation.This artifact has historically gravitated toward the hands of tyrants, cult leaders, and nefarious schemers. It does not merely compel obedience; it unravels the victim's agency, weaving the wielder's intent directly into their mind. Those who hold the staff feel a surge of magnetic presence, a dark charisma that bends the weak-willed before a single spell is even cast. It remains a relic of pure, unadulterated control.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Charisma: +1
- Saving Throws vs Enchantment School: +2

Charge abilities:
– Domination (Save vs. Wand -4 negates) three times per day
  Range: 40 ft.
  Duration: 12 hours
  Area of Effect: 1 creature

THAC0: +3
Damage: 1d6+3 (crushing)
Speed Factor: 1
Proficiency Type: Quarterstaff
Type: Two-handed
Requires:
 5 Strength

Weight: 2
"



